        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d216bda8-46db-5c91-ac19-07dd61807112",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John André, Benedict Arnold\n- Organizations: British Army, Continental Army\n- Places: West Point, New York\n- Events: American Revolutionary War, Arnold's attempted surrender of West Point\n\nFacts:\n- Benedict Arnold was born on January 14, 1741 (O.S. January 3, 1740) and died on June 14, 1801.\n- John André was born on 2 May 1750 and died on 2 October 1780.\n- Benedict Arnold was a general during the American Revolutionary War who first fought for the American Continental Army and later defected to the British Army.\n- John André was a British Army officer during the American Revolutionary War.\n- John André assisted Benedict Arnold's attempted surrender of the fort at West Point, New York, to the British.\n- The Continental Army hanged John André as a spy during the American Revolutionary War.",
